7.4 API Documentation
7.4.1 Authentication Endpoints
POST /api/auth/register - Register new user
POST /api/auth/login - User login
POST /api/auth/logout - User logout
7.4.2 User Management Endpoints
GET /api/users - Get all users (Admin only)
GET /api/users/:id - Get user by ID
PUT /api/users/:id - Update user
DELETE /api/users/:id - Delete user (Admin only)
7.4.3 Class Management Endpoints
GET /api/classes - Get all classes
POST /api/classes - Create class (Instructor/Admin)
GET /api/classes/:id - Get class details
PUT /api/classes/:id - Update class
DELETE /api/classes/:id - Delete class
7.4.4 Enrollment Endpoints
GET /api/enrollments/:classId - Get enrolled students
POST /api/enrollments - Enroll student
DELETE /api/enrollments/:id - Remove enrollment
7.4.5 Attendance Endpoints
POST /api/attendance/checkin - Check in to class
POST /api/attendance/checkout - Check out of class
GET /api/attendance/student/:studentId - Get student attendance
GET /api/attendance/class/:classId - Get class attendance
7.4.6 Messaging Endpoints
GET /api/messages - Get all conversations
GET /api/messages/:conversationId - Get messages
POST /api/messages - Send message
POST /api/conversations - Create conversation
7.5 Database Schema
7.5.1 Users Table
-id, username, email, password_hash, role, created_at, updated_at
7.5.2 Classes Table
-id, name, section, term, instructor_id, created_at
7.5.3 Enrollments Table
-id, student_id, class_id, enrolled_at
7.5.4 Attendance Table
-id, student_id, class_id, check_in_time, check_out_time, latitude, longitude, ip_address
7.5.5 Messages Table
-id, sender_id, recipient_id, conversation_id, content, timestamp, is_read
7.5.6 Conversations Table
-id, created_at, updated_at

7.6 Key Implementation Details
7.6.1 Authentication
-Uses JWT tokens for session management
-Token verified in Authorization header
-Role-based access control enforced via middleware

7.6.2 Geolocation Integration
-Calls Abstract API with user's IP address
-Returns latitude and longitude coordinates
-Stored with attendance records

7.6.3 Check-In Logic
-Enforces "one class at a time" rule
-Checks for existing active attendance before allowing check-in
-Captures geolocation data automatically

7.7 Adding New Features
7.7.1 To add a new API endpoint
-Create route handler in /server/routes/
-Implement logic in /server/controllers/
-Add database queries in /server/models/

7.7.2 To add a new UI component
-Create component in /client/src/components/
-Add routing in /client/src/App.js
-Connect to API in /client/src/services/

7.8 Testing
-Run backend tests: npm test
-Run frontend tests: cd client && npm test
-Test routes with Postman or curl

7.9 Common Issues and Troubleshooting
Problem: Database connection errors
-Verify .env credentials are correct
-Ensure database server is running

Problem: CORS errors
-Check CORS middleware configuration
Problem: Geolocation API failures
-Verify API key is valid
-Check rate limits

Problem: Authentication issues
-Clear cookies and cache

-Verify SESSION_SECRET is set
